      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What is Linux Kernel ? ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What is Linux Kernel ? ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "XpNmLoYP604Nz_R4SClW3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1910.4311296076967,
      "y": 1535.617154093081,
      "width": 627,
      "height": 575,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bGP",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2102186124,
      "version": 121,
      "versionNonce": 25927632,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785344449486,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Many people say:\n\"Linux is an Operating System.\"\nThat's only partially true.\nLinux technically refers to the kernel.\n\nThe kernel is the core component of the operating system.\n\nIt manages:\n\nCPU scheduling\nMemory\nDisk I/O\nNetworking\nProcesses\nDevice drivers\n\nApplications cannot directly access hardware.\n\nEverything goes through the kernel.\n\nPython -> Kernel -> CPU\nDocker -> Kernel -> Memory\nPostgreSQl -> Kernel ->  Disk",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Many people say:\n\"Linux is an Operating System.\"\nThat's only partially true.\nLinux technically refers to the kernel.\n\nThe kernel is the core component of the operating system.\n\nIt manages:\n\nCPU scheduling\nMemory\nDisk I/O\nNetworking\nProcesses\nDevice drivers\n\nApplications cannot directly access hardware.\n\nEverything goes through the kernel.\n\nPython -> Kernel -> CPU\nDocker -> Kernel -> Memory\nPostgreSQl -> Kernel ->  Disk",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "fB1MhTX9HO0sWqmVAr9l4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1863.9272233576967,
      "y": 2154.242154093081,
      "width": 275,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
