      "seed": 963976144,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 1021242832,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785345123203,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What is an Inode?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What is an Inode?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "5yBH4I2bXsUp8lfhW7Nkb",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1953.6694108576967,
      "y": 3658.742154093081,
      "width": 880,
      "height": 975,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bGy",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1794811184,
      "version": 153,
      "versionNonce": 1812460336,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785345310917,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "An inode is a data structure that stores metadata about a file.\nIt stores:\n\nFile size\nOwner\nGroup\nPermissions\nCreation time\nModification time\nFile type\nDisk block locations\n\nIt does NOT store the filename. This surprises almost everyone.\n\nThen where is the filename stored?\nThe directory stores: resume.pdf -> Inode 12345\nthe Inode store -> inode 12345 -> size, owner, permissions, disk block locations\n\nVisual Representation\nSuppose you have\n    resume.pdf\n\nInternaly ->\nDirectory\n\nresume.pdf\n      │\n      ▼\ninode 78215\n      │\n      ▼\nMetadata\n      │\n      ▼\nDisk Blocks\n\nNotice something interesting.\nThe filename and the actual file are different things.\nThe filename is only a pointer.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "An inode is a data structure that stores metadata about a file.\nIt stores:\n\nFile size\nOwner\nGroup\nPermissions\nCreation time\nModification time\nFile type\nDisk block locations\n\nIt does NOT store the filename. This surprises almost everyone.\n\nThen where is the filename stored?\nThe directory stores: resume.pdf -> Inode 12345\nthe Inode store -> inode 12345 -> size, owner, permissions, disk block locations\n\nVisual Representation\nSuppose you have\n    resume.pdf\n\nInternaly ->\nDirectory\n\nresume.pdf\n      │\n      ▼\ninode 78215\n      │\n      ▼\nMetadata\n      │\n      ▼\nDisk Blocks\n\nNotice something interesting.\nThe filename and the actual file are different things.\nThe filename is only a pointer.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "pZxkMRth_myy45AMMwfCH",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1950.4272233576967,
      "y": 4677.242154093081,
      "width": 121,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bGz",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 577012016,
      "version": 16,
      "versionNonce": 1911997392,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785345324781,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Hands On ->",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Hands On ->",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "JlYwKVk0_hj1bigLWcfTf",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1992.6733171076967,
      "y": 4709.730435343081,
      "width": 638,
      "height": 1125,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bH0",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1507956176,
      "version": 93,
      "versionNonce": 820393264,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785345505787,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Create a file -> touch linux.txt\nNow check inode -> ls -i\nExample -> 827364 linux.txt\n827364 is the inode number.\n\nNow\n    stat linux.txt\n\nYou'll see\n\ninode\nsize\npermissions\nowner\ntimestamps\n\nWhy Inodes Matter\nImagine\n project.zip is 10 GB\nYou rename it\n      mv project.zip backup.zip\n\nDoes Linux move 10 GB of data? -> No\nOnly the directory entry changes:\n\nOld\n\nproject.zip\n\n↓\n\ninode 8912\n\nNew\n\nbackup.zip\n\n↓\n\ninode 8912\n\nSame inode.\nSame data.\nOnly the filename changed.\nThis is why renaming a large file is almost instantaneous.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Create a file -> touch linux.txt\nNow check inode -> ls -i\nExample -> 827364 linux.txt\n827364 is the inode number.\n\nNow\n    stat linux.txt\n\nYou'll see\n\ninode\nsize\npermissions\nowner\ntimestamps\n\nWhy Inodes Matter\nImagine\n project.zip is 10 GB\nYou rename it\n      mv project.zip backup.zip\n\nDoes Linux move 10 GB of data? -> No\nOnly the directory entry changes:\n\nOld\n\nproject.zip\n\n↓\n\ninode 8912\n\nNew\n\nbackup.zip\n\n↓\n\ninode 8912\n\nSame inode.\nSame data.\nOnly the filename changed.\nThis is why renaming a large file is almost instantaneous.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "jqhv5zlDEDbnojExCUlaT",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1791.5444108576967,
      "y": 5872.441372843081,
      "width": 553.1659374999999,
      "height": 40.55468750000001,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
