      "updated": 1785347510866,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "touch original.txt -> create empty file\necho \"Linux Internals\" > original.txt -> overwrite or create original.txt file\nln original.txt hard.txt -> create hard link\nln -s original.txt soft.txt -> create soft link\nls -li -> it will give detail with inode\nstat original.txt -> displays detailed information (metadata) about a file\ncat hard.txt -> it will show content of hard.txt\ncat soft.txt -> it will show content of soft.txt\nrm original.txt -> it will remove original.txt\nnow soft.txt will be of no use\nrm -r directory_name -> it will delete directory and inside files and all\nrmdir directory_name -> it will delete directory if directory is empty else will give error\n\nstat -> The stat command displays detailed information (metadata) about a file or directory.\nMost people know:\n    ls -l\nExcellent question. stat is one of the most useful Linux commands, and it's asked surprisingly \noften in interviews.\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "touch original.txt -> create empty file\necho \"Linux Internals\" > original.txt -> overwrite or create original.txt file\nln original.txt hard.txt -> create hard link\nln -s original.txt soft.txt -> create soft link\nls -li -> it will give detail with inode\nstat original.txt -> displays detailed information (metadata) about a file\ncat hard.txt -> it will show content of hard.txt\ncat soft.txt -> it will show content of soft.txt\nrm original.txt -> it will remove original.txt\nnow soft.txt will be of no use\nrm -r directory_name -> it will delete directory and inside files and all\nrmdir directory_name -> it will delete directory if directory is empty else will give error\n\nstat -> The stat command displays detailed information (metadata) about a file or directory.\nMost people know:\n    ls -l\nExcellent question. stat is one of the most useful Linux commands, and it's asked surprisingly \noften in interviews.\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
